# Rich Menu Visual Builder Upgrade

## Goal Description
Replace the manual JSON input for Rich Menu areas with a visual, interactive builder. Users will select a template grid and click on areas to configure actions (Message, Link, Postback).

## Proposed Changes

### Library
#### [NEW] [rich-menu-templates.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/lib/rich-menu-templates.ts)
- Define standard templates with their grid coordinates:
    - `GRID_6_LARGE` (2x3)
    - `GRID_4_LARGE` (2x2)
    - `GRID_3_COMPACT` (1x3)
    - Etc.

### Components
#### [MODIFY] [create-rich-menu-dialog.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/rich-menu/create-rich-menu-dialog.tsx)
- Refactor into a multi-step wizard:
    1.  **Basic Info**: Name, ChatBar Text, Image URL.
    2.  **Template Selection**: Visual cards to pick a grid layout.
    3.  **Editor**:
        -   Preview of the uploaded image.
        -   Overlay grid based on selected template.
        -   Clicking a grid cell opens the **Action Dialog**.
- Remove the direct JSON text area.
- Auto-generate the JSON `areas` array upon submission based on the visual configuration.

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
1.  Open "Create Rich Menu" dialog.
2.  Enter basic info and valid image URL (2500x1686).
3.  Select a "Large 6-button" template.
4.  Click "Button 1" area -> Configure as "Message" -> "Test Message".
5.  Click "Button 2" area -> Configure as "Link" -> "https://google.com".
6.  Submit.
7.  Check network request or resulting database entry to ensure `areas` JSON is correctly formed with proper bounds and action objects.
